    "file": "php-src/Zend/zend_vm_execute.h",
    "description": "Null pointer dereference in the ASSIGN_REF opcode handler: after resolving variable/value pointers, the handler unconditionally does `ZVAL_COPY(EX_VAR(opline->result.var), variable_ptr)` when `RETURN_VALUE_USED(opline)` is true. For this PoV, `variable_ptr` can become invalid/null-like during reference assignment on crafted self-referential array/reference operations, and the copy reads from near-null (ASan read at 0x1), crashing at line ~27652.",
    "conditions": "Triggered by executing crafted PHP code (from the fuzzer input) that performs by-reference assignment with complex aliasing/self-reference (`$a[]=&$a; ... $a[0]=&gc_collect_cycles()`) and a dynamic variable name. This reaches `ZEND_ASSIGN_REF_SPEC_VAR_VAR_HANDLER` via normal `zend_execute` in the execute harness. The opcode path must have return value used for ASSIGN_REF, so the handler attempts to copy from `variable_ptr`; with the crafted state, that pointer is not valid, causing the null-deref read."
  },
